cd "/d/Frontend/Side Projects/Finance App" && node -e "
const fs=require('fs');
let p='docs/01-system-audit.md';let s=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');
const lines=s.split('\n');const i=lines.findIndex(l=>l.startsWith('| S2 |'));
lines[i]=lines[i].replace(/ \|\s*$/,'')+' **Updated 17 Oct (chat 5):** built as one default Card in the offer\\'s place: \"Verify your salary\", why (the wallet can\\'t see a salary paid into a bank), three steps as a plain numbered list (\`<ol>\`, not ListRow: the steps aren\\'t rows of data), and \"Start verification\" to a labelled placeholder (the pay-yourself placeholder, now taking its wording as props). No amounts, offer or decline wording |';
fs.writeFileSync(p,lines.join('\n'));
p='docs/progress.md';s=fs.readFileSync(p,'utf8');
const rep=(a,b)=>{if(!s.includes(a))throw new Error('missing: '+a.slice(0,70));s=s.replace(a,b)};
rep('## Decisions','### Chat 5, continued: S2, persona B\\'s home\n\n- **Proposed with better-layout and better-writing, kit only, then built.**\n- **The card:** one card in the offer\\'s place, \"Verify your salary\" (my Assumption\\'s name for it).\n  - \"Your salary is paid into a bank account, so your NovaPay wallet can\\'t see it. A salary advance needs your salary to be verified first.\"\n  - The steps: 1. Share a recent payslip or bank statement (the product reference\\'s documents). 2. We check it. 3. When it\\'s verified, this card shows what you can do next.\n  - \"Start verification\" (primary).\n- **What it leaves out:** amounts, the offer, decline wording, \"unlock\", a reason for needing the salary (invented policy), and how long checking takes (unknown).\n- **The stub:** \"Start verification\" opens the existing placeholder screen, which now takes its wording as props: \"Placeholder: verify your salary / This screen isn\\'t built yet. Nothing has been shared.\" The file keeps the name \`PayYourselfPlaceholder.jsx\` (renaming means deleting a file, which needs my OK).\n- **Checked in the app:** persona B\\'s card, the placeholder and back, and the pay placeholder unchanged. At 360×640 the button ends at 438px of 582px.\n\n## Decisions');
rep('**Lock-screen previews (5.4): skipped, my call.**','**S2:** step 3 is option A (\"this card shows what you can do next\"), which doesn\\'t promise an offer and doesn\\'t hint at a decline. The placeholder screen is reused.\n\n**Lock-screen previews (5.4): skipped, my call.**');
rep('  - **Persona B\\'s home now shows no advance card at all**','  - ~~**Persona B\\'s home now shows no advance card at all**~~ *Resolved in chat 5: S2 is built.*');
rep('2. **Persona B\\'s home card** (S2, verify salary) is still not built.','2. ~~**Persona B\\'s home card**~~ *Built in chat 5.*');
rep('- *From the S13 rejection:*','- *From S2, noted, not fixed:*\n  - **\`PayYourselfPlaceholder.jsx\` now serves two placeholders**, so its name is narrower than its use. A rename needs my OK.\n  - **The reviewer panel crashed during the hot reload** that dropped 20 Aug: the open page still had 20 Aug selected. It isn\\'t reachable from a fresh load, but the panel assumes its date exists.\n- *From the S13 rejection:*');
fs.writeFileSync(p,s);" && npm run check 2>&1 | tail -1 && git add src/screens/Home.jsx src/screens/PayYourselfPlaceholder.jsx src/App.jsx docs/01-system-audit.md docs/progress.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
S2: persona B's home, "Verify your salary" as a step before any advance

Persona B is paid into a bank account, so the wallet can't see their
income. Rather than letting them apply and be declined (principle 2), Home
shows one card in the offer's place: "Verify your salary", why, the steps
(share a recent payslip or bank statement, the product reference's
documents; we check it; when it's verified, this card shows what you can do
next), and "Start verification".

No amounts, offer or decline wording; no "unlock", no invented reason for
needing the salary and no checking time. Step 3 promises nothing either way
(my choice, option A). "Start verification" opens the existing labelled
placeholder, which now takes its wording as props; the pay-yourself
placeholder is unchanged. Checked in the app at 390x844 and 360x640.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
git log --oneline -1 && git status --short

